//Skirt: cream pleated skirt with orange embroidery and a frilled petticoat
# Skirt: s from the waist (z=8.66) to the hem (z=1.61); t is the angle from the front, + toward her
# left. sa(s) is its half-width: one straight line from the corset to the hem. Seen from the side the front hangs
# nearly flat and the back is full, so the depth is dk(s,t) times the half-width: 0.57 at the front, 0.75
# to 1 at the back from the waist to the hem. 40 knife pleats (spl), 9 degrees apart as traced: each rises slowly
# to its edge and drops back sharply, cut into the skirt (the edges stay on sa) and deepening to 5% of the
# radius at the hem. Arch meshes a surface with at most 60 steps a side, too few for 40 pleats, so the skirt is
# built in ten sectors of 3.5 to 4.4 pleats each; a thin line is drawn in each pleat where the skirt shows.
# sz(h) is s at height h.
sa(s)=0.43+0.0579*ln(1+exp((s-0.057)/0.02))
stp(q)=min(1,max(0,q))^2*(3-2*min(1,max(0,q)))
fk(s)=0.57-0.04*stp((s-0.5)/0.15)+0.07*stp((s-0.78)/0.14)
gk(s)=0.75+0.25*s
dk(s,t)=(fk(s)+gk(s))/2-(gk(s)-fk(s))/2*cos(t)
sz(h)=(8.66-h)/7.05
spl(s,t)=1-0.05*(0.2+0.8*s)*(0.5+0.645*atan(0.7*sin(40*t)/(1-0.7*cos(40*t))))
(sa(s)*spl(s,t)*sin(t),-sa(s)*spl(s,t)*dk(s,t)*cos(t),8.66-7.05*s,s,0,1,t,(-0.56),0) | ref=underskirt1 color=#ddd3c2
(sa(s)*spl(s,t)*sin(t),-sa(s)*spl(s,t)*dk(s,t)*cos(t),8.66-7.05*s,s,0,1,t,0,0.56) | ref=underskirt2 color=#ddd3c2
(sa(s)*spl(s,t)*sin(t),-sa(s)*spl(s,t)*dk(s,t)*cos(t),8.66-7.05*s,s,0,1,t,0.56,1.24667) | ref=underskirt3 color=#ddd3c2
(sa(s)*spl(s,t)*sin(t),-sa(s)*spl(s,t)*dk(s,t)*cos(t),8.66-7.05*s,s,0,1,t,1.24667,1.93333) | ref=underskirt4 color=#ddd3c2
(sa(s)*spl(s,t)*sin(t),-sa(s)*spl(s,t)*dk(s,t)*cos(t),8.66-7.05*s,s,0,1,t,1.93333,2.62) | ref=underskirt5 color=#ddd3c2
(sa(s)*spl(s,t)*sin(t),-sa(s)*spl(s,t)*dk(s,t)*cos(t),8.66-7.05*s,s,0,1,t,2.62,3.14159) | ref=underskirt6 color=#ddd3c2
