//Hair
# Her hair flows from the crown. A lock is described by t, from the crown (0) down to the end of
# the longest hair (1): up to t = 0.15909 it lies on a dome around the head (ha is the angle from the
# crown), below that it falls. hzz(t) is the height, hrx(t) and hry(t) are the half-axes of the ellipse the
# hair lies on at that height: they follow the dome, then keep clear of the shoulders, capelet, arms, book
# and skirt and flare out toward the ends (fitted by the generator). hu(t) is 0 on the dome and grows to 1
# down the fall. hdw keeps a lock's width steady as the hair spreads.
ha(t)=1.5708*min(1,t/0.15909)
hu(t)=max(0,t-0.15909)/0.84091
hzz(t)=12.15+0.825*cos(ha(t))-8.14591*max(0,t-0.15909)
hrx(t)=0.725*sin(ha(t))+34.73898*max(0,t-0.15909)^2+(-80.66494)*max(0,t-0.18909)^2+66.1993*max(0,t-0.21909)^2+(-47.88559)*max(0,t-0.24909)^2+78.53613*max(0,t-0.27409)^2+(-153.23162)*max(0,t-0.29909)^2+349.21997*max(0,t-0.32409)^2+(-183.33589)*max(0,t-0.34909)^2+(-311.40909)*max(0,t-0.37409)^2+442.83447*max(0,t-0.39909)^2+(-296.08572)*max(0,t-0.42909)^2+145.89942*max(0,t-0.46909)^2+(-44.51582)*max(0,t-0.51909)^2+(-72.23632)*max(0,t-0.58909)^2+221.45701*max(0,t-0.67909)^2+(-316.40632)*max(0,t-0.77909)^2+234.04981*max(0,t-0.87909)^2
hry(t)=0.815*sin(ha(t))+34.5262*max(0,t-0.15909)^2+(-79.12478)*max(0,t-0.18909)^2+60.27607*max(0,t-0.21909)^2+(-27.52259)*max(0,t-0.24909)^2+23.72654*max(0,t-0.27409)^2+(-31.91523)*max(0,t-0.29909)^2+58.40202*max(0,t-0.32409)^2+107.10773*max(0,t-0.34909)^2+(-265.30522)*max(0,t-0.37409)^2+101.19633*max(0,t-0.39909)^2+32.82453*max(0,t-0.42909)^2+16.35638*max(0,t-0.46909)^2+(-80.73192)*max(0,t-0.51909)^2+69.07069*max(0,t-0.58909)^2+(-41.70495)*max(0,t-0.67909)^2+96.36859*max(0,t-0.77909)^2+(-127.40853)*max(0,t-0.87909)^2
hdw(t)=1.54/(1.54+69.26518*max(0,t-0.15909)^2+(-159.78972)*max(0,t-0.18909)^2+126.47536*max(0,t-0.21909)^2+(-75.40819)*max(0,t-0.24909)^2+102.26267*max(0,t-0.27409)^2+(-185.14685)*max(0,t-0.29909)^2+407.62198*max(0,t-0.32409)^2+(-76.22817)*max(0,t-0.34909)^2+(-576.71431)*max(0,t-0.37409)^2+544.0308*max(0,t-0.39909)^2+(-263.26118)*max(0,t-0.42909)^2+162.25581*max(0,t-0.46909)^2+(-125.24774)*max(0,t-0.51909)^2+(-3.16563)*max(0,t-0.58909)^2+179.75206*max(0,t-0.67909)^2+(-220.03773)*max(0,t-0.77909)^2+106.64129*max(0,t-0.87909)^2)
# Her head is tilted and turned (see the generator); a lock turns with it where it lies on the head and
# hangs straight below. hb(t) is 1 on the head and eases to 0 by t = 0.24909; hs and hk are the sine and
# one minus the cosine of the head's turn times hb, and hm scales the lock with the head where it lies on it.
hb(t)=1-min(1,max(0,(t-0.15909)/0.09))^2*(3-2*min(1,max(0,(t-0.15909)/0.09)))
hs(t)=sin(0.14069*hb(t))
hk(t)=1-cos(0.14069*hb(t))
hm(t)=1-0.18*hb(t)
# A lock is a tube around its own flow line. lpc is the angle of that line around the head: a starting
# angle pb+p0 (0 = straight back, + toward her left) whose part p0 closes up by sg as the hair spreads (sg = 1
# falls straight down, sg = 0 fans out over the shoulders; pb is 0 for the back and pi for the front), a drift dr, and a wave of size am that grows down the
# lock. lrc is how far the line stands off the hair surface: its layer la, and the wave again a quarter turn
# later, so the lock snakes in and out as well as side to side. Across the lock (w runs around it) lwd is
# the half-width and lth the thickness, a crescent lcs with three ridges that is flat underneath. ltp tapers
# the lock toward its end te, and lq runs 0..1 over the last stretch, where the tip turns through three
# quarters of a circle: sideways like a hook, or outward like a scroll.
ltp(t,te)=min(1,max(0,te-t)/0.13)^0.6
lq(t,te)=max(0,1-max(0,te-t)/0.08)
lcs(w)=(0.65*sin(w)+0.35*abs(sin(w)))*(0.78+0.22*cos(2*pi*cos(w)))
lpc(t,pb,p0,sg,dr,am,kk,ph)=pb+p0*(1-sg*(1-hdw(t)))+dr*hu(t)+am*hu(t)^1.5*sin(kk*hu(t)+ph)
lrc(t,la,am,kk,ph)=la*min(1,t/0.04)+0.6*am*hu(t)^1.5*cos(kk*hu(t)+ph)
lwd(t,te,hw)=hw*ltp(t,te)*hdw(t)
lth(t,w,te,th)=th*ltp(t,te)*lcs(w)*min(1,t/0.04)
# A dark cap and an inner sheet under the locks, so no gap shows skin. The cap stops higher above her left
# eye and a little higher above her right eye, where the forehead shows between the bangs as on the sheet.
(0.81191*(0.7105*sin(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2)))*cos(v))+0.0572*(0.14+0.7987*sin(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2)))*sin(v))+(-0.09969)*(12.15+0.8085*cos(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2))))+1.11963,(-0.05677)*(0.7105*sin(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2)))*cos(v))+0.818*(0.14+0.7987*sin(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2)))*sin(v))+0.00697*(12.15+0.8085*cos(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2))))+(-0.05693),0.09993*(0.7105*sin(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2)))*cos(v))+0.81389*(12.15+0.8085*cos(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2))))+2.10307,u,0,1,v,-pi,pi) | ref=hairCap color=#ac5232
